{
  "slug": "preguntas-negacion",
  "number": 5,
  "part": 2,
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Questions and negation",
  "tagline": "¿Qué, dónde, cuándo…?, the upside-down marks, and Spanish double negatives.",
  "goal": "Ask questions with or without question words, answer in the negative, and use nunca, nada, nadie and ninguno correctly, including double negatives.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "si-no",
      "title": "Yes / no questions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No «do / does» and usually no change of order: a statement becomes a question with **intonation** (and the marks ¿ ? in writing)."
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "Hablas español. → ¿Hablas español?", "tr": "You speak Spanish. → Do you speak Spanish?" },
            { "fr": "¿Tu hermano vive aquí? / ¿Vive aquí tu hermano?", "tr": "Does your brother live here?", "note": "both orders are fine" },
            { "fr": "Vienes mañana, ¿verdad? / ¿no?", "tr": "You're coming tomorrow, aren't you?" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "interrogativos",
      "title": "Question words",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Spanish", "English", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["*qué*", "what", "*¿{Qué} haces?*"],
            ["*cuál / cuáles*", "which, what (from options)", "*¿{Cuál} es tu número?*"],
            ["*quién / quiénes*", "who", "*¿{Quién} es?*"],
            ["*dónde* · *adónde* · *de dónde*", "where · where to · where from", "*¿{De dónde} eres?*"],
            ["*cuándo*", "when", "*¿{Cuándo} llegas?*"],
            ["*cómo*", "how", "*¿{Cómo} estás?*"],
            ["*cuánto / cuánta / cuántos / cuántas*", "how much, how many", "*¿{Cuántos} años tienes?*"],
            ["*por qué*", "why", "*¿{Por qué} estudias español?* — *{Porque}…*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Qué or cuál with «ser»",
          "text": "English «What is your name / number / address?» uses **cuál**: *¿Cuál es tu dirección?* Use *qué es* only to ask for a definition: *¿Qué es un aguacate?*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negacion",
      "title": "Negation and double negatives",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Put **no** before the verb (and before object pronouns): *No hablo francés. No lo sé.*"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Positive", "Negative", "Example"],
          "rows": [
            ["*siempre* (always)", "*nunca* (never)", "*{No} como {nunca} carne. / {Nunca} como carne.*"],
            ["*algo* (something)", "*nada* (nothing)", "*{No} quiero {nada}.*"],
            ["*alguien* (someone)", "*nadie* (nobody)", "*{No} vino {nadie}.*"],
            ["*algún / alguna* (some)", "*ningún / ninguna* (no, none)", "*{No} tengo {ningún} problema.*"],
            ["*también* (too)", "*tampoco* (neither)", "*A mí {tampoco}.*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "Double negatives are correct",
          "text": "If the negative word comes **after** the verb, keep *no* before it: *No veo nada* (literally «I don't see nothing»). If it comes first, drop *no*: *Nada me gusta*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
